# Example environment variables for Project-CIP
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. DO NOT commit your real `.env` with secrets to version control.

# Azure / OpenAI settings (example placeholders)
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY="<YOUR_AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY>"
AZURE_EMBEDDING_API_KEY="<YOUR_AZURE_EMBEDDING_API_KEY>"
AZURE_EMBEDDING_DEPLOYMENT="text-embedding-3-small"
AZURE_DEPLOYMENT_NAME="gpt-35-turbo"
AZURE_EMBEDDING_OPENAI="https://<YOUR_AZURE_RESOURCE>.openai.azure.com/openai/deployments/text-embedding-3-small/embeddings?api-version=2023-05-15"
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT="https://<YOUR_AZURE_RESOURCE>.cognitiveservices.azure.com/openai/deployments/gpt-35-turbo/chat/completions?api-version=2025-01-01-preview"

# Optional: path to Chroma DB directory
CHROMA_DB_DIR="langchain-openai/chroma_db"

# Example local settings
#DEBUG=true

## Notes
- Replace angle-bracketed placeholders with your real keys and endpoints.
- Keep this file in the repository; copy to `.env` and fill with secrets on your machine or CI/CD service.
- For Posit Cloud deployments, set these variables in the project settings rather than committing them.
